Caveat
======

1. If you are having trouble installing the package, check whether the path to
your PHCpack executable was set correctly. You can check this by typing the
following command:

options PHCpack

If it is wrong, you can update it by putting the absolute path into the
init-PHCpack.m2 file, For example, if the executable phc is located in
C:/cygwin/PHC, then the line inside the init-PHCpack.m2 file will look like
this:

"path" => "C:/cygwin/PHC/" .

Alternately, the path could be set when loading the package using the following
command:

loadPackage ("PHCpack", Configuration=>{"path"=>"C:/cygwin/PHC/","PHCexe"=>"./
phc"})

2. The current version 1.8 of PHCpack.m2 was developed with version 1.9 of
Macaulay2 and with version 2.4.17 of phc.

