cascade -- runs a cascade of homotopies to get witness sets for the variety
***************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        cascade L
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of polynomials
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note StartDimension: cascade_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStartDimension=>_pd_pd_pd_
        rp, => ..., default value -1, Option to specify the dimension to begin
        searching for positive dimensional components
      * *note Verbose: cascade_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, option to specify whether additional output is
        wanted
  * Outputs:
      * a *note numerical variety: (NAGtypes)NumericalVariety,, containing the
        witness sets for each pure-dimensional variety contained in zero set of
        L.
  * Consequences:
      * Writes the system to temporary file
      * Invokes the command phc -c (with option 0)
      * Stores output of phc in temporary file
      * Parses and outputs the solutions.

Description
===========

Given a list of generators of an ideal I, this function creates an embedding
and then runs a cascade of homotopies. The output is a *note NumericalVariety:
(NAGtypes)NumericalVariety, that contains a *note WitnessSet:
(NAGtypes)WitnessSet, for each pure dimensional variety contained in V(I).



+------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y,z];           |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : L = { z*(x+y), z*(x-y) };|
+------------------------------+
|i3 : WitSets = cascade(L)     |
|                              |
|o3 = WitSets                  |
|                              |
|o3 : NumericalVariety         |
+------------------------------+
|i4 : W=first WitSets#2        |
|                              |
|o4 = W                        |
|                              |
|o4 : WitnessSet               |
+------------------------------+

The function cascade extends the ring of the inputted system with slack
variables beginning with zz.  Each witness set in contains the equations,
points, and slices of the embedded system.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : W#Equations                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {-2} | (-.995325+.0965773ii)zz1+(-.356282+.934379ii)zz2-xz-yz |         |
|     {-2} | (.0656456-.997843ii)zz1+(.408711+.912664ii)zz2-xz+yz   |         |
|     {-1} | -zz1+(.999978-.00663642ii)zz2                          |         |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : PolySystem                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : W#Points                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = {{-.665048-.161006*ii, 1.14439+.924941*ii, 0, 0, 0}}                    |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : VerticalList                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : W#Slice                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = | -.247841-.968801ii .968065+.250699ii .397263-.917705ii                |
|     | -.536026+.844201ii .680343-.732894ii -.997495-.0707353ii              |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     .474694-.880151ii  -.0126009-.999921ii -.867121-.498097ii |             |
|     -.280228-.959934ii -.998091+.0617632ii -.964058-.265691ii |             |
|                                                                             |
|                2         6                                                  |
|o7 : Matrix CC    <-- CC                                                     |
|              53        53                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

