factorWitnessSet -- applies monodromy to factor a witness set into irreducible components
*****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        factorWitnessSet(w)
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note witness set: (NAGtypes)WitnessSet,, properly embedded with
        slack variables
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Verbose: factorWitnessSet_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value false, option to specify whether additional output
        is wanted
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of witness sets, every
        element of the list is irreducible
  * Consequences:
      * writes the system to temporary files,
      * invokes the command phc -f (with option 2),
      * uses monodromy to factor,
      * uses default settings of path trackers ,
      * stores output of phc in temporary file,
      * parses and outputs the solutions.

Description
===========

A witness set is irreducible if there exists a path between any two of its
generic points that does not pass through a singularity.

We illustrate the factorization via the twisted cubic and a line.



+-------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y,z]; f = {(x^2-y)*(x-1), x^3 - z};|
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (w,ns) = topWitnessSet(f,1);                |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : w                                           |
|                                                 |
|o4 = w                                           |
|                                                 |
|o4 : WitnessSet                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : L = factorWitnessSet(w)                     |
|found 2 irreducible factors                      |
|                                                 |
|o5 = L                                           |
|                                                 |
|o5 : NumericalVariety                            |
+-------------------------------------------------+

