interactive -- flag to run phc -p or phc -m in interactive mode
***************************************************************

Description
===========

There are too many options for the path trackers in phc -p to wrap them
properly within the trackPaths() method. With interactive turned on, the user
can tune all parameters of the path trackers, in the same way as running phc
-p.

The option interactive is also supported to run the polyhedral homotopies to
solve random coefficient systems with phc -c, in the mixedVolume function with
the option StartSystem set to true.

