isCoordinateZero -- checks if coordinate has absolute value less than a given tolerance
***************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isCoordinateZero(sol,k,tol)
  * Inputs:
      * sol, a *note point: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint,, solution to a polynomial
        system
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, index of coordinate
      * tol, a *note real number: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,, tolerance on the absolute
        value of the k-th coordinate
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if the k-th
        coordinate of solution has absolute value less than tol, false
        otherwise

Description
===========

A solution has a zero k-th coordinate when the abs function evaluates to a
number less than the given tolerance.



+-------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y];                                |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = { x^3*y^5 + y^2 + x^2*y, x*y + x^2 - 1};|
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : fSols = solveSystem(f, randomSeed=>3);      |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : fSols/print                                 |
|{-1, 0}                                          |
|{1, 0}                                           |
|{-.894935+.624334*ii, .143333-1.14868*ii}        |
|{-.764107, -.544612}                             |
|{.742585+.425943*ii, .270685-1.00715*ii}         |
|{-.894935-.624334*ii, .143333+1.14868*ii}        |
|{1.33076-.335184*ii, -.62414+.513163*ii}         |
|{.742585-.425943*ii, .270685+1.00715*ii}         |
|{-1.59272, .964857}                              |
|{1.33076+.335184*ii, -.62414-.513163*ii}         |
|                                                 |
|o4 = {, , , , , , , , , }                        |
|                                                 |
|o4 : List                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isCoordinateZero(fSols_0,1,1.0e-10)         |
|                                                 |
|o5 = true                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------+

Good values for the tolerance are relative to the accuracy and the condition
number of the solution. To improve the accuracy of a solution, apply *note
refineSolutions: refineSolutions, with a higher working precision.



See also
========

  * *note refineSolutions: refineSolutions, -- refines solutions of a system by
    increasing working precision
  * *note zeroFilter: zeroFilter, -- returns solutions with k-th coordinate
    less than the given tolerance
  * *note nonZeroFilter: nonZeroFilter, -- returns solutions with coordinate
    larger than given tolerance

