isWitnessSetMember -- tests whether a point belongs to a solution set
*********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isWitnessSetMember(W,p)
  * Inputs:
      * W, a *note witness set: (NAGtypes)WitnessSet,, positive dimensional,
        properly embedded with slack variables
      * p, a *note point: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Verbose => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false, whether additional output is wanted, including the input and
        solution file names used by phc.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if p is a member of
        the solution set of W, false otherwise
  * Consequences:
      * Invokes the command phc -f (with option 1)

Description
===========

Uses numerical homotopy methods to test whether the point p belongs to the
variety associated to the witness set W.

Although W should be properly embedded, p should be given in the coordinates of
the original system.



+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x11,x22,x21,x12,x23,x13];               |
