numThreads -- the number of threads in the path tracker
*******************************************************

Description
===========

Tracking many solution paths is a pleasingly parallel computation. A
multithreaded path tracker has a number of threads working on a queue of path
tracking jobs.  Every path tracking job can be computed without communication
overhead.  For sufficiently large problems, the speedup can as large as the
number of threads.

Functions with optional argument named numThreads:
==================================================

  * *note mixedVolume(...,numThreads=>...):
    mixedVolume_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmnumThreads=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- option to set the
    number of threads when solving a start system
  * *note solveSystem(...,numThreads=>...):
    solveSystem_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmnumThreads=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- option to set the
    number of threads
  * *note trackPaths(...,numThreads=>...):
    trackPaths_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmnumThreads=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- Option to define the
    number of threads in the path tracker.

